rrington</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Primary prevention of cardiovascular disease with atorvastatin in type 2 diabetes in the Collaborative Atorvastatin Diabetes Study (CARDS) : multicentre randomised placebo-controlled trial</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2004</year><volume>364</volume><fpage>685</fpage><lpage>96</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15325833</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crouse</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Grobbee</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>O&#x02019;leary</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Measuring Effects on intima media Thickness: an Evaluation Of Rosuvastatin in subclinical atherosclerosis - the rationale and methodology of the METEOR study</article-title><source>Cardiovasc Drugs Ther</source><year>2004</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>231</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15229392</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crouse</surname><given-names>JR</given-names><suffix>3rd</suffix></name><name><surname>Raichlen</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Riley</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><collab>METEOR Study Group</collab><article-title>Effect of rosuvastatin on progression of carotid intima-media thickness in low-risk individuals with subclinical atherosclerosis: the METEOR Trial</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2007</year><volume>297</volume><fpage>1344</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17384434</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name></person-gro